Running Mocha tests


  Subscription milestone 2 — currency, configuration and registry
    1) mints six-decimal simulated currency only through its owner
    ✔ preserves the asset registry and assigns the issuer, token, caps and immutable dates
    2) rejects zero supply
    3) rejects zero price
    4) rejects zero softCap
    5) rejects zero start
    6) rejects zero end
    7) rejects EOA/zero tokens, wrong decimals, wrong issuer, overflow and inconsistent caps/times
    8) blocks outsiders, another authorised issuer and revoked issuers from offering this asset

  Subscription milestone 3 — escrow and time window
    9) requires issuer, whitelist, allowance, positive bounded deposits and permits partial funding
    10) enforces exact start/end boundaries and rejects deposits at start
    ✔ rejects underfunded subscriptions even when donated tokens supply the balance
    11) checks eligibility, multiples, balances and allowances without changing accounting on failure
    ✔ accepts oversubscription, accumulates top-ups and counts distinct subscribers only

  Subscription milestones 4–5 — allocation, settlement and independent payouts
    12) blocks early and repeated finalisation and all premature settlement/claims/refunds/recovery
    ✔ settles 1800/1400/800 into 450/350/200, protects unsettled deposits and refunds (89ms)
    ✔ handles 1400 mUSD undersubscription and protects unclaimed entitlements during recovery
    13) fails with 700 mUSD, refunds fully after revocation and recovers all inventory
    14) preserves refunds when claims are blocked by revocation or pause, then allows reapproved claims
    15) prevents repeated payouts, settlement, claiming others and unauthorised issuer actions
    16) never credits stablecoin donations as issuer earnings

  Subscription rounding and bounded model invariants
    ✔ three equal subscribers receive two of seven units each; dust unlocks only after all settle (40ms)
    ✔ conservatively fails when gross demand exceeds soft cap but rounded funding is not guaranteed
    ✔ allows zero-token subscribers a full refund without erasing others' entitlement
    ✔ conserves exact accounting under seeded top-ups and payout ordering (7) (164ms)
    ✔ conserves exact accounting under seeded top-ups and payout ordering (41) (135ms)
    ✔ conserves exact accounting under seeded top-ups and payout ordering (2026) (133ms)
    ✔ handles multiplication beyond 256 bits using full-precision mulDiv


